# core/data/talk/grammar/en/open_manners.tlk - replies to thanks, apologies and introductions
# (owner: TK; T5b package T5B-OPEN). Clean in any room, no register word, no romance. Rule names
# start with o_. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py.

# ---- THANK: "you're welcome" in many ways ------------------------------------------------------
@rule core.thank.o_plain act: answer
  "Any time! I mean it. Well, most times."
  "You're welcome! It was my pleasure. And a little bit my job."
  "Don't mention it. Actually, do. To everyone."
  "Of course! That's what friends are for, and neighbours, and pie."
  "No need to thank me. But I won't stop you."
@rule core.thank.o_joke act: joke
  "Thanks accepted! Please deposit them in the jar by the door."
  "I'll take that in cash, cake, or compliments. Or all three."
  "You're welcome! That'll be one hundred hugs. Kidding, fifty."
  "Thanks noted! I'm putting it on my wall of fame. It's a small wall."
@rule core.thank.o_tease act: tease
  "Wow, manners! Who raised you? Someone good."
  "You said thanks! Quick, someone write it down."
  "Look at you, being all polite. It suits you. Mostly."
@rule core.thank.o_back act: backchannel
  "Mm-hm. Yep, of course. Any time."
  "Yeah, yeah. It was nothing. It was a little something."
@rule core.thank.o_dismiss act: dismiss
  "It was nothing. Really. Don't make a fuss."
  "Pfft. Stop. You'll make me blush, and I hate that."
@rule core.thank.o_polite guard: polite act: answer
  "You're most welcome. It was no trouble at all."
  "Think nothing of it, {you}. The pleasure was entirely mine."
  "How kind of you to say. I'm delighted to have helped."
@rule core.thank.o_blunt guard: blunt act: answer
  "Yeah, yeah. You're welcome. Don't make it weird."
  "Sure. Whatever. Glad it helped."
@rule core.thank.o_flat guard: flat act: answer
  "You're welcome. {.}This is me, glowing."
  "Mm. No problem. I felt a small joy."
@rule core.thank.o_loud guard: loud act: answer
  "YOU'RE WELCOME! ANY TIME! I MEAN ANY TIME!"
@rule core.thank.o_elder guard: elder act: answer
  "Oh, you're welcome, dear. It's nice to be of use."
  "Don't mention it, young one. I had nothing else on."
@rule core.thank.o_quirky guard: quirky act: answer
  "You're welcome! The spoon sends its regards."
@rule core.thank.o_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "You're welcome! Do I get a sticker? A small one?"
  "No problem! I'm very helpful, everybody says so. Sometimes."
  "You're welcome! Patrol is always happy to help."
@rule core.thank.o_friend guard: rel=friend act: answer
  "Anytime, friend. You'd do the same for me. Probably."
  "Oh, stop. We're friends. That's the deal."
@rule core.thank.o_best guard: rel=best act: answer
  "Don't thank me. You'd do it for me. You'd do it better."
@rule core.thank.o_rival guard: rel=rival act: tease
  "Thanks? From you? I'm flattered and suspicious."
@rule core.thank.o_happy guard: mood=happy act: answer
  "[HAPPY]You're welcome! It made my day, too!"
@rule core.thank.o_sad guard: mood=sad act: answer
  "[SAD]You're welcome. It's nice to be thanked. It helps."
@rule core.thank.o_tired guard: mood=tired act: answer
  "[SLEEPY]Mm. Welcome. I'll feel proud when I wake up."

# ---- APOLOGIZE: accepting, brushing off, teasing ---------------------------------------------------
@rule core.apologize.o_accept act: answer
  "It's all right. Truly. Everyone slips sometimes."
  "Apology accepted! Let's agree to be silly together."
  "Thanks for saying so. I feel much better already."
  "It's forgotten. Well, filed in a drawer under fine."
  "Okay, I appreciate that. Don't do it again. Or do, politely."
@rule core.apologize.o_comfort act: comfort
  "Hey, come on. We all mess up. Have a biscuit."
  "It's okay, {you}. Really. Let's put it down and walk away from it."
  "Don't be so hard on yourself. You're a good egg. Mostly."
@rule core.apologize.o_dismiss act: dismiss
  "Forget it. It's already forgotten. Look, it's gone."
  "Pfft, it's fine. I wasn't even counting. Much."
@rule core.apologize.o_joke act: joke
  "Sorry accepted! That'll be one cookie as a fine."
  "Apology noted. Let's write it in the logbook, next to the goose."
  "Oh, now you're sorry? Let me find my tiny violin."
@rule core.apologize.o_complain act: complain
  "Well. It's about time. I was starting to sulk."
  "Hmph. Fine, I'll forgive you. I'll keep a note, though."
@rule core.apologize.o_polite guard: polite act: answer
  "Please, think nothing of it. It's quite forgotten."
  "That's very gracious. Apology accepted, with my thanks."
@rule core.apologize.o_blunt guard: blunt act: answer
  "Fine. Done, moving on. Don't make it a speech."
  "Yeah, okay. Sorry accepted. Just don't repeat it."
@rule core.apologize.o_flat guard: flat act: answer
  "It's fine. {.}I've forgiven you. Look at my face, see, fine."
@rule core.apologize.o_elder guard: elder act: answer
  "Oh, hush, dear. I've forgotten already. It's one of my talents."
@rule core.apologize.o_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: answer
  "Okay! I forgive you. Do you want to play now?"
  "It's okay. I'm not mad. I was only a tiny bit mad."
@rule core.apologize.o_rival guard: rel=rival act: complain
  "You? Apologising? Quick, someone check the sky."
@rule core.apologize.o_friend guard: rel=friend act: comfort
  "We're friends. That's what we do. We mess up and we fix it."

# ---- INTRODUCE: hello, what's your deal, and the player's own name ---------------------------------------
@rule core.introduce.o_plain act: greet
  "Nice to meet you, {you}! I'm {me}. Pleased to be pleased."
  "Hello, {you}! Welcome to the neighbourhood. I hope you like fog."
  "{you}! What a name. I'll write it on my hand so I won't forget."
  "Hi, {you}! I'm {me}. We're going to be friends, I can tell."
  "Oh, hello! I'm {me}. Don't worry, I only bite on Wednesdays."
@rule core.introduce.o_ask act: ask_about
  "Nice to meet you! So where are you from? And why?"
  "Hello, {you}! What do you like to do, when no one's looking?"
  "Hi! Tell me something about you. A fun fact, or a sad one."
  "Lovely to meet you! What brings you here? Fate, or the bus?"
@rule core.introduce.o_joke act: joke
  "{you}! I'll remember that, probably. Don't test me."
  "Oh, a new friend! My collection's almost complete. I need a goose."
  "Nice to meet you, {you}! I'm {me}, a professional neighbour."
@rule core.introduce.o_tease act: tease
  "{you}? Hmm, I'll allow it. It's a fine name."
  "Pleased to meet you! You seem shiny. I'll keep an eye on you."
@rule core.introduce.o_polite guard: polite act: greet
  "How do you do, {you}? I'm {me}. It's a pleasure."
  "Delighted to make your acquaintance. Please, call me {me}."
@rule core.introduce.o_blunt guard: blunt act: greet
  "Hi. I'm {me}. Don't expect a hug."
  "{you}, right? Okay. I'm {me}, fine."
@rule core.introduce.o_quirky guard: quirky act: greet
  "Hello, {you}! I'm {me}, and this is my hat, Gerald."
@rule core.introduce.o_kid guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: greet
  "Hi! I'm {me}! I'm this many years old, a lot!"
  "Hello, {you}! Do you want to be my friend? You can say no."
  "I'm {me}! I have a rock collection! Want to see?"
@rule core.introduce.o_elder guard: elder act: greet
  "How nice to meet you, {you}. I'm {me}. I've been here forever."
@rule core.introduce.o_happy guard: mood=happy act: greet
  "[HAPPY]Hi, {you}! I'm {me}! I love meeting people!"
